# D45 — m5 power: phantom-input storm kill (kernel tag d45).
# Spec (binding): .specs/bob-m5-power-audio-spec.md §2 (ADR-m5-WS1 option W1),
# §5.1.1; DELTA-NOTES: patches/kernel/DELTA-NOTES.md "D45".
#
# THE DEFECT: at screen-off idle the event0 device delivered ~2.9 Hz phantom
# KEY_VOLUMEDOWN press/release pairs. Every idle wake from that chain kept
# the platform out of deep sleep (60-min uptime/realtime baseline 0.66).
#
# THE FIX (four dead-bolts, all required — the build gates assert each):
#  1. arch/arm/mach-mt6582/q5/keypad/mtk_kpd.h (K1): DELETE the
#     KPD_PMIC_RSTKEY_MAP (=KEY_VOLUMEDOWN) define. The Q5 fchrkey pin is
#     unwired; D22 PTY evidence places VOLDOWN on matrix slot [1]
#     (cust_kpd.h keymap {[0]=KEY_VOLUMEUP,[1]=KEY_VOLUMEDOWN}), so the PMIC
#     rstkey mapping could only ever be the phantom reporter. The #ifdef'd
#     users of the define (kpd.c kpd_pmic_rstkey_handler/probe keybit,
#     hal_kpd.c kpd_pmic_rstkey_hal) compile out cleanly.
#  2. drivers/misc/mediatek/power/mt6582/pmic_mt6323.c (K2): the fchrkey IRQ
#     is disabled at BOTH enable points — cust_pmic_interrupt_en_setting()
#     (upmu_set_rg_int_en_fchrkey 1->0) and both 0x166,[1:1] register pokes
#     in PMIC_INIT_SETTING_V1() (0x166,0x1->0x166,0x0). pwrkey stays enabled
#     (upmu_set_rg_int_en_pwrkey(1) untouched) — the build gate greps it.
#  3. drivers/misc/mediatek/keypad/kpd.c (K3): the matrix tasklet no longer
#     reports keys directly (old code reported ANY change bit with zero
#     confirmation, and hal_kpd.c's per-sample "register =" dump printed on
#     every scan). Instead it only samples the matrix; a delayed work item
#     re-reads it kpd_glitch_ms (default 150, module param) later and reports
#     only bits stable across both samples that differ from the last reported
#     state. Unstable bits are counted (kpd_glitch_drops) and logged
#     printk_ratelimited — this is the §6 storm-death-certificate metric.
#     AEE 5s/15s logic, hrtimers and the backlight handler are unchanged;
#     suspend cancels the pending work; resume re-syncs the baselines
#     without reporting (no stuck key for a press spanning suspend).
#     No msleep/schedule_timeout in the tasklet; system workqueue only.
#  4. drivers/misc/mediatek/keypad/mt6582/hal_kpd.c: the "register = %x…"
#     scan dump (printed on EVERY matrix sample at line ~317) is gated on a
#     new module param kpd_show_scan (default 0). The press/release printk
#     stays on the existing kpd_show_hw_keycode flag (§6 field prints).
#
# HOST TEST: build/test_kpd_filter.py G1–G6 (runs in the 82 kernel chain,
# before flash). §8 R2 revert criterion: kpd_glitch_ms=0 restores old
# reporting shape (single-sample, minus the direct tasklet path).
--- a/arch/arm/mach-mt6582/q5/keypad/mtk_kpd.h
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-mt6582/q5/keypad/mtk_kpd.h
