+ * matrix and reports exactly the bits that agree between the two samples
+ * (tasklet S1 in kpd_pending_state, work S2 below) AND differ from the last
+ * reported state. A phantom glitch pair that self-cancels inside the window
+ * leaves its bits back at the baseline: they never agree-with-and-differ, so
+ * nothing is reported. Genuine holds differ from the baseline at both
+ * samples, so press and release are still delivered
+ * (host build/test_kpd_filter.py G1–G6). */
+static void kpd_glitch_work_func(struct work_struct *work)
 {
+	u16 s2[KPD_NUM_MEMS];
+	unsigned long dropped = 0;
 	int i, j;
-	bool pressed;
